[issue.1832]
number = 1832
title = "[Coherence] The payer-grant property suite now only checks that symbols are absent, but the spec still says it proves a 2000-grant round-trip and canonical decoding"
revision = "a910fdedd579e63379ae6c2e4d4971990d28f8ad"
verdict = "spec-edit"
evidence = "The specification must replace the obsolete codec guarantees in req.1041 (spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:18462), acceptances 1.41.1 and 1.41.2 (spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:100724 and spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:100732), and done task 1.9.3 (spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:144228) with the weak-reference absence checks actually implemented at tests/fuzz/lxp_prop_payer_grant.c:20 and tests/fuzz/lxp_prop_payer_grant.c:27 by commit 563747fa29d0415d9d586ce5db51024bc5ca7214 after commit 52fda45db6899c35154e4efcb98d45adc10e85f2 deleted the codec, consistent with req.1047 (spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:18496) and tests/repair_22_39_76.kvx:30, and retire the still-stable decode, encode and verifier rows at spec/layerx-merge/interfaces.kvx:18579, spec/layerx-merge/interfaces.kvx:18589 and spec/layerx-merge/interfaces.kvx:22914 while retaining the already-retired authorization-message row at spec/layerx-merge/interfaces.kvx:14628; Makefile:2672 runs both cases through core-test-all at Makefile:2680 and .github/workflows/ci.yml:178."
close_comment = "The kernel payer-grant codec was retired with RECEIVE, and these cases now check null weak references rather than seeded round-trip or canonical decoding properties. Requirement 1041, acceptances 1.41.1/1.41.2 and completed task 1.9.3 need to describe those absence probes, and the encode, decode and verifier interface entries need retirement; the authorization-message entry is already retired."
